#: Metad.md:1
msgid "Sampling the guessed path"
msgstr "推定 Path の Sampling"

#: Metad.md:3
msgid ""
"We can use the parameterized guessed path in production simulations using "
"any sampling method relying on the use of CVs. For instance, metadynamics "
"(metad) simulations can be conducted to reconstruct the free energy surface "
"in the Path CV space. Here, we will show how to set up a metad simulation "
"leveraging Path CVs. Note that this is only an illustrative example, on how "
"to set up and run the simulation, with no intention of achieving here a "
"converged free energy surface."
msgstr ""
"パラメータ化した Path は、CV を使う任意の Sampling 法の本計算に使えます。例えば Metadynamics (metad) で "
"Path CV 空間の自由エネルギー表面を再構成できます。ここでは設定・実行例だけを示し、表面の収束は目指しません。"

#: Metad.md:5
msgid ""
"An important aspect here is that you may need to renumber the atom number "
"column (second column) of the *REPARAM_FINAL.pdb* file. This is because the "
"atom indices in *REPARAM_FINAL.pdb* are consistent with the lighter version "
"of the system, i.e. no hydrogens, no membrane lipids, and no waters. Since "
"we are now going to conduct a simulation of the whole system, atom "
"information for the atoms inside the *REPARAM_FINAL.pdb*, particularly the "
"atom index, need to be consistent with those in the whole system. Assuming "
"we need to achieve such renumbering, we produce a "
"*REPARAM_FINAL_renumber.pdb* file."
msgstr ""
"*REPARAM_FINAL.pdb* の第2列の Atom Number を振り直す必要がある場合があります。*REPARAM_FINAL.pdb* "
"は水素・Membrane "
"Lipid・水を除いた軽量な系と整合する番号ですが、これからは全系をシミュレーションするためです。*REPARAM_FINAL.pdb* "
"内の原子情報、特に Index を全系と一致させます。振り直したファイルを *REPARAM_FINAL_renumber.pdb* とします。"

#: Metad.md:7
msgid ""
"We now have all we need to set up a metad simulation. We will bias the "
"$S(\\mathbf{R})$ and $Z(\\mathbf{R})$ CVs. We take metad simulation "
"parameters from this publication: https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.9b00450 "
"Specifically, we set Gaussian width to 0.1 for $S(\\mathbf{R})$ and 1 $Å^2$ "
"for $Z(\\mathbf{R})$, Gaussian height to 0.2 kcal/mol, temperature to 310 K,"
" bias factor to 15, and Gaussians deposition time to 1 ps. Finally, we can "
"re-sample remaining closer to the configurational space sampled by the "
"original SMD that we have used to parameterize the guess path. To this end, "
"we can limit the region of the phase space accessible during the simulation "
"by placing a suitable ``UPPER_WALL`` on $Z(\\mathbf{R})$, e.g. at 3.0 $Å^2$."
" Fill in the following plumed template to perform such a metad simulation:"
msgstr ""
"準備ができたので、$S(\\mathbf{R})$ と $Z(\\mathbf{R})$ に Bias を加えます。パラメータは "
"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.9b00450 に従い、Gaussian 幅を $S(\\mathbf{R})$ "
"で0.1、$Z(\\mathbf{R})$ で1 $Å^2$、高さを0.2 kcal/mol、温度を310 K、Bias Factor "
"を15、追加間隔を1 ps とします。元の SMD が探索した領域の近くを再 Sampling するため、$Z(\\mathbf{R})$ に "
"``UPPER_WALL`` を、例えば3.0 $Å^2$ に置けます。次の入力を完成させてください。"

#: Metad.md:32
msgid "To run the simulation with the GROMACS md engine, just enter:"
msgstr "GROMACS MD エンジンでは、次で実行します。"

#: Metad.md:37
msgid ""
"As in any metad simulation, plumed will produce a *HILLS* file, which you "
"can use to reconstruct the free energy surface using the **``sum_hills``** "
"module, as follows:"
msgstr "通常の metad と同じく *HILLS* が生成され、**``sum_hills``** で自由エネルギー表面を再構成できます。"

#: Metad.md:42
msgid ""
"This results in a *fes.dat* file, that we can finally plot to visualize the "
"reconstructed free energy surface. Here is the result of a 50 ns metad "
"simulation:"
msgstr "*fes.dat* を描画し、再構成した表面を可視化できます。50 ns の metad の結果です。"

#: Metad.md:44
msgid "![fes](figures/fes_tmp.png \"Figure\")"
msgstr "![FES](figures/fes_tmp.png \"Figure\")"

#: Metad.md:46
msgid ""
"In usual production scenarios, you may envisage a more generous exploration "
"of the configurational space around the reference path. For instance, you "
"can adapt the above plumed template to repeat the simulation with a larger "
"```UPPER_WALL```. Here is the resulting free energy surface using 9.0 $Å^2$,"
" with the same simulation time of 50 ns:"
msgstr ""
"通常の本計算では、参照 Path 周辺をより広く探索してもよいでしょう。例えば ```UPPER_WALL``` を広げます。同じ50 ns で9.0 "
"$Å^2$ を使うと、次の表面になります。"

#: Metad.md:48
msgid "![fes](figures/fes_tmp_largerwall.png \"Figure\")"
msgstr "![FES](figures/fes_tmp_largerwall.png \"Figure\")"

#: Metad.md:50
msgid "Note that:"
msgstr "次の点に注意してください。"

#: Metad.md:52
msgid ""
"Expanding the allowable range of $Z(\\mathbf{R})$ for sampling might promote"
" a broader, non-local search for additional routes along the reference path "
"($Z(\\mathbf{R})=0$). As long as these routes remain reasonably close to it,"
" they could suggest alternative and possibly more favourable mechanisms for "
"the binding process."
msgstr ""
"$Z(\\mathbf{R})$ の許容範囲を広げると、参照 "
"Path（$Z(\\mathbf{R})=0$）に沿う別経路を広く非局所的に探せます。適度に近い範囲なら、結合の代替機構や、より有利な機構が見つかる可能性があります。"

#: Metad.md:54
msgid ""
"The further you go on $Z(\\mathbf{R})$, the less meaningful and more "
"degenerate will become the mapping on $S(\\mathbf{R})$, so that sampling "
"will become inconvenient and, most remarkably, less efficient the "
"exploitation of your computational resources."
msgstr ""
"$Z(\\mathbf{R})$ が大きいほど $S(\\mathbf{R})$ の写像は意味を失い、縮退が増えます。Sampling "
"が不便になり、特に計算資源の利用効率が低下します。"

#: Metad.md:56
msgid ""
"It is also important to note that the metad simulation time of 50 ns used "
"here is solely intended for illustrative purposes, as no attempts have been "
"made to assess the convergence of the free energy or evaluate the "
"statistical error (the range covered by $S(\\mathbf{R})$ was not even fully "
"sampled!). We recommend dedicated Plumed Tutorials or Masterclasses for a "
"thorough exploration of these issues. To provide an order of magnitude, a "
"metad sampling of approximately 2 $\\mu \\text{s}$ was utilized in this "
"study https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.9b00450 to obtain meaningful results."
msgstr ""
"50 ns の metad は例示のみです。自由エネルギーの収束や統計誤差は評価しておらず、$S(\\mathbf{R})$ 全範囲さえ完全には "
"Sampling していません。詳しくは専用の Plumed Tutorial・Masterclass "
"を参照してください。規模の目安として、https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.9b00450 では有意な結果に約2 $\\mu"
" \\text{s}$ の metad を使いました。"
